  "details": "   * SECURITY UPDATE: excessive memory use with relative CRL distribution\n     point names\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-35189.patch: build the full name of a\n       nameRelativeToCRLIssuer distribution point only while matching a\n       CRL instead of for every parsed certificate in\n       crypto/x509v3/v3_crld.c, crypto/x509v3/v3_purp.c and\n       crypto/x509/x509_vfy.c\n     - CVE-2026-35189\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: DTLS retransmission corrupts a suspended write\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-84782.patch: reset init_off before\n       retransmitting a message in ssl/statem/statem_dtls.c and skip the\n       retransmission while a write is still parked in ssl/d1_lib.c\n     - CVE-2026-84782",
